FetchReach-v4 is a goal-conditioned robotic manipulation task. A 7-DoF Fetch arm must move its gripper (end-effector) to a desired 3D target position.

The native observation is a dict with keys:
- observation: robot proprioceptive state (10 dims)
- achieved_goal: current gripper position in 3D (3 dims)
- desired_goal: target gripper position in 3D (3 dims)

In this project, flatten_observation is enabled, so the policy input is a 16-dimensional vector:
- state[0:10] = observation
- state[10:13] = achieved_goal
- state[13:16] = desired_goal

The action space is Box(-1, 1, (4,), float32):
- action[0]: x-axis Cartesian control of the end-effector
- action[1]: y-axis Cartesian control of the end-effector
- action[2]: z-axis Cartesian control of the end-effector
- action[3]: gripper open/close command

The policy is a linear policy with 68 parameters and works as follows:
action = state @ W + b, where
- state has shape (16,)
- W has shape (16, 4)
- b has shape (4,)

Parameter mapping:
- W[i, j] = params[4 * i + j], for i in [0..15], j in [0..3]
- b[j] = params[64 + j], for j in [0..3]

Equivalent grouped view:
- params[0..3]   = weights from state[0] to 4 actions
- params[4..7]   = weights from state[1] to 4 actions
- ...
- params[60..63] = weights from state[15] to 4 actions
- params[64..67] = action biases

With reward_type=dense, reward is shaped by goal distance and is highest near 0 when the gripper reaches the target.
The objective is to maximize cumulative episodic reward by minimizing end-effector distance to the desired goal quickly and stably.
